{"name":"Badlands Sunset","hex":"#936a5b","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"badlands","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An arid terrain characterized by severe erosion of sedimentary rocks.","An arid region of Western Canada characterized by significant erosion and odd land formations containing dinosaur and other fossils."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/badlands"},{"term":"sunset","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The moment each evening when the sun disappears below the western horizon.","The changes in color of the sky before and after sunset."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To phase out."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sunset"}],"entries":[{"title":"Badlands","blocks":[{"text":"Badlands are a type of dry terrain where softer sedimentary rocks and clay-rich soils have been extensively eroded. They are characterized by steep slopes, minimal vegetation, lack of a substantial regolith, and high drainage density. Ravines, gullies, buttes, hoodoos and other such geologic forms are common in badlands."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Chinle_Badlands.jpg/330px-Chinle_Badlands.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Badlands","wikidata":"Q272921"},{"title":"Sunset","blocks":[{"text":"Sunset is the disappearance of the Sun at the end of the Sun path, below the horizon of the Earth due to its rotation. As viewed from everywhere on Earth, it is a phenomenon that happens approximately once every 24 hours, except in areas close to the poles. The equinox Sun sets due west at the moment of both the spring and autumn equinoxes. As viewed from the Northern Hemisphere, the Sun sets to the northwest in the spring and summer, and to the southwest in the autumn and winter; these seasons are reversed for the Southern Hemisphere."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Full_cycle_of_a_Sunset_on_the_high_plains_of_the_Mojave_Desert.jpg/330px-Full_cycle_of_a_Sunset_on_the_high_plains_of_the_Mojave_Desert.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunset","wikidata":"Q166564"},{"title":"Sunset (color)","blocks":[{"text":"The color sunset is a pale tint of orange. It is a representation of the average color of clouds when the sunlight from a sunset is reflected from them."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Sunset_2007-1.jpg/330px-Sunset_2007-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunset_(color)","wikidata":"Q11696368"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/A030%2C_Theodore_Roosevelt_National_Park%2C_North_Dakota%2C_USA%2C_2001.jpg/330px-A030%2C_Theodore_Roosevelt_National_Park%2C_North_Dakota%2C_USA%2C_2001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/A030%2C_Theodore_Roosevelt_National_Park%2C_North_Dakota%2C_USA%2C_2001.jpg/330px-A030%2C_Theodore_Roosevelt_National_Park%2C_North_Dakota%2C_USA%2C_2001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Caprock atop hoodoos in Theodore Roosevelt National Park, North Dakota, U.S.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA030%2C_Theodore_Roosevelt_National_Park%2C_North_Dakota%2C_USA%2C_2001.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Cheltenham_Badlands_panorama1.jpg/500px-Cheltenham_Badlands_panorama1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Cheltenham_Badlands_panorama1.jpg/1280px-Cheltenham_Badlands_panorama1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.or